Service members who joined after January 2018 are automatically enrolled in the Blended Retirement System (BRS). Members who joined earlier either chose BRS or kept the legacy High-3 plan, and those who kept legacy cannot currently switch. Legacy High-3 pays 2.5% × years of service × High-3 average pay (50% at 20 years), with no Thrift Savings Plan (TSP) matching and no benefit for those who leave before 20 years. BRS lowers the multiplier to 2.0% (40% at 20 years) but adds up to 5% TSP matching after three years of service plus a continuation pay bonus. BRS members who leave before 20 years keep their TSP balance and any vested matching. Your service's personnel or retirement office can confirm which system you are under, and the [Military OneSource BRS overview](https://militaryonesource.mil/financial-legal/military-retirement/blended-retirement-system/) lays out the enrollment rules.